      "content": "I see. The \"controlled volume\" and \"clean lines\" point is interesting. To be totally honest though, when my clients talk about \"looking professional,\" they often get a sense that there's a specific standard they're being measured against. Like, if someone is wearing a hijab or has very traditional, non-Western hair, do you think they have to work harder to prove they're \"authoritative\" compared to someone with a more conventional, straight blonde or brunette style? How should they navigate that to make sure they aren't seen as \"unprofessional\" because of their cultural grooming?",
